\nFinally, we evaluate at $t=2,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,2}=\\frac{3}{4(2)}=\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266530 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266531 13194139533929 true] [17592186266530 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266532 13194139533929 true] [17592186266530 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533929 true] [17592186266530 1041 "field-1" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266530 1104 #edb/ref 17592186266532 13194139533929 true] [17592186266530 1110 #uuid "7a358d85-f4d7-515d-9468-6665228a47f5" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266531 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266531 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533929 true] [17592186266531 1111 #uuid "2ccaa9ac-6693-54a9-8b45-1e346d481a03" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266532 1034 "\\frac{3}{8}" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533929 true] [17592186266532 1111 #uuid "858cb3db-5191-5d55-a47d-21207204175d" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266533 1017 #edb/ref 17592186266534 13194139533929 true] [17592186266533 1089 "q-352390" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266533 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533929 true] [17592186266533 1100 "A curve has parametric equations $x={t}^{5}+1,\\,y=\\frac{35}{6}{t}^{6}+2{t}^{5}+9.$ Given that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=7t+2,$ calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ at the point where $t=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,2}=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266533 1113 #uuid "84d2b5b2-de55-52a6-af4a-f2e1349bfd06" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266533 1145 "To compute $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}},$ we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=7t+2,$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}({t}^{5}+1)=5{t}^{4}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(7t+2)}{5{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(7)}{5{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5{t}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate at $t=2,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,2}=\\frac{7}{5({2}^{4})}=\\frac{7}{80}.\n$$" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266535 13194139533929 true] [17592186266534 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533929 true] [17592186266534 1041 "field-1" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266534 1104 #edb/ref 17592186266535 13194139533929 true] [17592186266534 1110 #uuid "94b4cd57-ce0f-52f0-a0f2-0292fcc15d3f" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266535 1034 "\\frac{7}{80}" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266535 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533929 true] [17592186266535 1111 #uuid "6f11ff6b-5cc9-55ab-a138-b73419ae3487" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266536 1017 #edb/ref 17592186266537 13194139533929 true] [17592186266536 1089 "q-78947" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266536 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533929 true] [17592186266536 1100 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations $x={t}^{3}-1,\\,y=3{t}^{6}+2$ where $t$ is a real number. Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}.$" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266536 1113 #uuid "d91b9b6d-416f-56f9-8f80-d7518f3295a7" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266536 1145 "To find the first derivative, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=18{t}^{5}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{18{t}^{5}}{3{t}^{2}}=6{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the second derivative, we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(6{t}^{3})}{3{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18{t}^{2}}{3{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266538 13194139533929 true] [17592186266537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266539 13194139533929 true] [17592186266537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266540 13194139533929 true] [17592186266537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266541 13194139533929 true] [17592186266537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266542 13194139533929 true] [17592186266537 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533929 true] [17592186266537 1041 "selection" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266537 1104 #edb/ref 17592186266541 13194139533929 true] [17592186266537 1110 #uuid "4ccbf2d7-ea9b-53a8-b333-f600349584c4" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266538 1034 "9" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266538 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533929 true] [17592186266538 1111 #uuid "3697ea5a-686e-516d-b7fd-7445fbc0660a" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266539 1034 "\\frac{6}{t}" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266539 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533929 true] [17592186266539 1111 #uuid "b5739e7c-53f2-5c7f-9652-c0a0c6b6259c" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266540 1034 "\\frac{t}{6}" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266540 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533929 true] [17592186266540 1111 #uuid "a18de0a6-94fe-57d2-a4d0-ab6bbe39c322" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266541 1034 "6" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266541 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533929 true] [17592186266541 1111 #uuid "319a4c57-e962-59a0-91f3-8d5b92eaaf01" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266542 1034 "6t" 13194139533929 true] [17592186266542 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533929 true] [17592186266542 1111 #uuid "0da525df-b37b-5e53-ac19-e0730966ddfe" 13194139533929 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-122888" 17592186266515 "q-122888/selection" 17592186266516 "q-122888/selection/503c2bb1c4db16493a63b6f7f0c97524202c88631bb4d91dc4723a4282dc72b2" 1759